Description
AIM
The aim of this experiment is to perform classification on multiple datasets using ID3, J48, Naive Bayes, and k-NN classifiers in WEKA, evaluate their performance using entropy, Kappa statistic, confusion matrix, ROC curves, and extract classification rules to determine the most suitable classifier for each dataset.

Problem Statement
For the datasets weather.nominal.arff, iris.arff, and glass.arff, perform the following tasks:

Run ID3 and J48 classifiers and study the decision tree, accuracy, Kappa statistic, and confusion matrix.
Compute entropy for the root node of the decision tree and observe information gain.
Extract IF-THEN rules from the J48 decision tree.
Run Naive Bayes and k-NN (IBk) classifiers and evaluate their performance.
Plot ROC curves for each classifier.
Compare all classifiers and identify the best and worst performing models for each dataset.
