Algorithm
Step 1: Load Dataset
Open WEKA Explorer.
Click Open File.
Load weather.nominal.arff.
Observe the number of instances, attributes, and class attribute.
Step 2: Run ID3
Go to Classify tab.
Select trees → Id3.
Choose 10-Fold Cross Validation.
Click Start.
Observe the generated decision tree and evaluation metrics.
Step 3: Run J48
Select trees → J48.
Keep default settings.
Run with 10-fold cross validation.
Observe the generated decision tree and classification results.
Step 4: Compute Entropy
Entropy Formula:

[ H(S) = - \sum p_i \log_2 p_i ]

For the Weather dataset:

[ H(S) = -\left(\frac{9}{14}\log_2\frac{9}{14}\right) -\left(\frac{5}{14}\log_2\frac{5}{14}\right) ]

[ H(S) \approx 0.940 ]

Step 5: Extract Rules from J48
Example Rules:

IF outlook = sunny AND humidity = high THEN play = no
IF outlook = sunny AND humidity = normal THEN play = yes
IF outlook = overcast THEN play = yes
IF outlook = rainy AND windy = TRUE THEN play = no
IF outlook = rainy AND windy = FALSE THEN play = yes
Step 6: Run Naive Bayes
Select bayes → NaiveBayes.
Run cross-validation.
Record accuracy, precision, recall, and confusion matrix.
Step 7: Run k-NN (IBk)
Select lazy → IBk.
Set k = 3 or use the default value.
Run cross-validation.
Observe performance metrics.
Step 8: Plot ROC Curves
Right-click the classifier result.
Select Visualize Threshold Curve.
Choose the target class.
Observe ROC curve and AUC value.
Step 9: Repeat for Iris and Glass
Load iris.arff.
Run all classifiers.
Load glass.arff.
Run all classifiers.
Collect and compare results.
